{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789319192,"nonce":"R3H53yMCwrecYILuPs/qP+1Ygxo=","message":"Re-tested on the NUC (x86_64, Linux) at c563239: 14065400 with no projection failures across tiered default, WLIFT_TIER1=off, WLIFT_TIER1=cranelift with --jit-threshold 1 --opt-threshold 5, --jit-threshold 1, and --mode jit, three runs each. The inline-cache numbering was the cause: every walker counted SuperCall as a slot and the backends counted only the calls left after devirtualisation, so a getter after a super call in the same body read its neighbour's entry. Fixed in 7c0f603 (git-bug 46620c4), with tests/e2e.rs e2e_calls_after_a_super_call_keep_their_inline_caches as the reproducer.","files":null}]}